# Device Compatibility (Android)

Guide for handling Gen 1 (Ray-Ban Meta) and Gen 2 (Meta Ray-Ban Display) glasses in the DAT SDK.

## Supported devices

| Device | Generation | Available since | Key feature |
|--------|-----------|-----------------|-------------|
| Ray-Ban Meta | Gen 1 | SDK v0.1.0 | Camera, audio, open-ear speakers |
| Meta Ray-Ban Display | Gen 2 | SDK v0.4.0 | Camera, audio, built-in display |

Both generations support the same streaming API — `StreamSession`, `VideoFrame`, and `capturePhoto()` work identically for Gen 1 and Gen 2.

## Checking device compatibility

Before streaming, check that the connected device is compatible with your SDK version:

```kotlin
lifecycleScope.launch {
    Wearables.devicesMetadata[deviceId]?.collect { metadata ->
        when (metadata.compatibility) {
            DeviceCompatibility.COMPATIBLE -> {
                // Device is ready to use
            }
            DeviceCompatibility.DEVICE_UPDATE_REQUIRED -> {
                // Glasses firmware is too old — prompt user to update
                val name = metadata.name.ifEmpty { deviceId.toString() }
                showError("$name requires a firmware update")
            }
        }
    }
}
```

## Discovering devices

```kotlin
lifecycleScope.launch {
    Wearables.devices.collect { deviceIdentifiers ->
        // deviceIdentifiers contains all paired/connected devices (Gen 1 and Gen 2)
    }
}
```

## Selecting a device

### Auto-select (recommended)

`AutoDeviceSelector` picks the best available device automatically and filters out
incompatible devices by default:

```kotlin
val selector = AutoDeviceSelector()
```

To include all devices regardless of compatibility:

```kotlin
val selector = AutoDeviceSelector(filter = { true })
```

To prefer Gen 2 over Gen 1, supply a custom ranking function:

```kotlin
val selector = AutoDeviceSelector(
    rank = { deviceId ->
        val metadata = Wearables.devicesMetadata[deviceId]?.value
        when (metadata?.deviceType) {
            DeviceType.META_RAYBAN_DISPLAY -> 0   // Gen 2 first
            DeviceType.RAYBAN_META         -> 1   // Gen 1 second
            else                           -> 2
        }
    }
)
```

### Target a specific device

```kotlin
val selector = SpecificDeviceSelector(deviceIdentifier = knownDeviceId)
```

## Reading device metadata

```kotlin
val metadata = Wearables.devicesMetadata[deviceId]?.value

// Device name (e.g., "My Frames")
val name = metadata?.name

// Firmware version string
val firmware = metadata?.firmwareVersion

// Compatibility status
val compat = metadata?.compatibility
```

## MockDeviceKit: simulating Gen 1

```kotlin
val mockDeviceKit = MockDeviceKit.getInstance(context)
mockDeviceKit.enable()

val gen1Device = mockDeviceKit.pairRaybanMeta()   // Simulates Ray-Ban Meta (Gen 1)
gen1Device.powerOn()
gen1Device.unfold()
gen1Device.don()
```

